deliberation.plan_raw:
The user wants a comprehensive plan for launching an AI sepsis‑risk CDS tool in a multi‑hospital system, covering clinical safety, legal/regulatory exposure, and financial structure. All three specialists are needed to address the distinct domains of medical device validation, regulatory compliance, and pricing/ROI.

{
  "core_question": "How to design a defensible first version of an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool across clinical safety, legal/regulatory exposure, and financial structure for a 12‑hospital system?",
  "rationale": "Clinical safety requires medical device validation expertise; legal must handle FDA/CMO/CMS compliance and liability; finance needs to model subscription economics.",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "What are the key components and steps to ensure clinical safety, effectiveness, and workflow integration for a first‑release AI sepsis risk scoring CDS tool in a multi‑hospital system?",
    "legal": "What legal and regulatory requirements must be met for deploying an AI-based sepsis risk score CDS tool across 12 hospitals, including FDA classification, CMS reimbursement eligibility, and data privacy compliance?",
    "finance": "How should the health system structure the annual per‑seat subscription pricing for an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool to balance affordability, revenue, and return on investment across 12 hospitals?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "FDA SaMD guidance updates post-2023, CMS reimbursement policies for CDS tools, recent state privacy laws affecting data use"
}
